el copied from an example rather than chosen — h5 on a page whose sections are h2. Only the number changes.","value":"1 title"},{"id":"buttons","on":true,"label":"Put the buttons on the house style","why":"1 button uses a Bootstrap variant rather than btn-info, so the same kind of action is drawn three different ways across the site. Only the class changes.","value":"1 button"},{"id":"solo","on":true,"label":"Let a lone card use the full width","why":"1 row holds a single card in a part-width column, so it takes a third or a half of the page and the rest is blank. A row of one is not a grid.","value":"1 card"},{"id":"searchtable","on":true,"label":"Let a long table be searched","why":"1 table runs to fifteen rows or more, so finding one row means reading every row. The theme already loads the search behaviour on every page and switches it on for any table marked this way — 26 tables across the site already are, including the contact directory. It adds a search box and a \"show 25 entries\" menu above the table, makes the column headings sortable, and pages below twenty-five rows at a time — which leaves all but the longest tables whole. Nothing is reordered and nothing changes until someone types.","value":"1 table"},{"id":"eyebrow","on":true,"label":"Eyebrow: \"Federal Emergency Relief Programs\"","why":"Taken from the parent page, /fedrelief."}],"mechanical":["empty paragraphs removed: 2","loose text wrapped in a paragraph: 59","paragraph inside a table cell unwrapped: 59","tables normalised to the house shape: 1","redundant bold inside a heading removed: 1","action links marked: 17","blockhead heading level normalised to h2: 1"],"findings":[{"name":"card-row-holding-one-card","n":1,"eg":["a grid row with one card in it"]}],"safe":true,"audit":{"alias":"/fedrelief/crf","title":"Coronavirus Relief Fund (CRF)","changed":"2026-04-06T22:50:29+00:00","words":141,"bytes":5179,"fixes":["empty paragraphs removed: 2","loose text wrapped in a paragraph: 59","paragraph insid